Revision history for Tie::Cache::Autoupdater

0.10
        First version, released on an unsuspecting world.
0.20
        Added new attribute - "clone". Delete unnecessary warn message when key doesn't exist
0.21
        Bugfix. Check data type before returned dclone reference
0.22
        Bugfix. FIRSTKEY and NEXTKEY returned cached values instead of key
        names, so "keys %cache" listed values and "each %cache" could not be
        used at all. Iterating an empty cache also created an entry under an
        empty key. They now return key names, as the tie interface requires.

        Rewrote the documentation and the README, and documented behaviour
        that was previously undescribed: how a source's return value is
        normalised, what happens when a source dies, what "clone" does and
        does not copy, and how the standard hash operations behave.

        Test suite extended to cover the whole module (statements, branches,
        conditions and subroutines). Verified on perl 5.26 - 5.42.

        Added a LICENSE file with the full license text and fixed the license
        declared in Makefile.PL: it said Artistic 2.0, while the documentation
        has always said "the same terms as Perl itself" (Artistic 1.0 or GPL).

        Removed the empty TODO file from the distribution.
